{
  "requirement": "The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is satisfied.**\n\n**Implementation**\n- `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` builds the expected text for each `{req}` block. It takes the block body (`block.body_start..block.body_end`) through `crate::without_options(...)`, then `.trim()`. That is all the Markdown inside the fenced directive, with leading and trailing whitespace removed. The only thing dropped is the `:impl:` and `:test:` option lines, which the anchors requirement treats as metadata. `without_options` in `src/lib.rs` (marked `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.requirement_text`) does the stripping.\n- `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`, marked `{impl}` at the specific check) compares the evidence file's `requirement` string with `expected.text` by exact equality. A mismatch pushes the error `\"{label}: requirement text changed at <source>\"` plus a compact diff. So changed requirement text is reported, as the requirement demands.\n- The same function rejects an empty text field. `collect_definitions` separately reports a definition with no text. This is a small extra, but it is consistent with the schema checks.\n- The `{impl}` markers cover the comparison (`validate_evidence_file`) and the text extraction (`without_options`). Extraction is the only other code that shapes the expected text. `preprocess_book` also calls `without_options` to build rendering text, but that is not part of this requirement.\n\n**Tests** (each marked `{test}` for this requirement in `src/evidence.rs`)\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` records a multi-paragraph requirement that contains a nested code fence and a `{req}` reference. The evidence file validates with no errors, so the full inner Markdown matches.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` records stale text (\"Old text.\") against \"First.\". It asserts that `requirement text changed`, `- Old text.` and `+ First.` are reported. It also asserts that a non-string `requirement` is reported and that an empty requirement body is flagged.\n- `anchored_files_must_be_completely_covered_and_resolvable` shows that `:impl:` and `:test:` option lines are excluded from the expected text. Evidence containing only \"Ready MUST hold.\" produces no \"text changed\" error.\n- The `anchor_options_are_metadata_not_body_text` test in `src/lib.rs` also checks nested-fence behavior of `without_options` directly. It is marked only for the anchors requirement, not this one.\n\n**Minor observation:** no test explicitly adds surrounding whitespace to a block body. The `.trim()` is simple and visible in the code, so this does not amount to a gap.",
